WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.250
On the deep Pacific floor, mostly
4,000 to 6,000 metres down,

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.030
lie fields of metal-rich nodules.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.030
They hold nickel, copper,
cobalt and manganese.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.210
Seventeen exploration contracts
cover one Pacific zone.

5
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.850
Rules for mining them have
been in development since 2014.

6
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.250
On land, drill rigs pull up cores of rock.

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.370
So is there a fixed amount
of copper in the ground?

8
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.170
Or does it depend on who is counting?

9
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:33.370
In this mission, you'll sort stock
resources from flow resources.

10
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.710
Then you'll follow a
resource through time,

11
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.950
from first drill hole to peak and decline.

12
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: find out whether the amount
of copper in the ground is really fixed.
